            "en": "In 80 AD, Emperor Titus inaugurated the magnificent Flavian Amphitheater, famously known as the Colosseum. Standing four stories tall and capable of seating more than fifty thousand roaring spectators, it represented the technological zenith of imperial architecture. A complex subterranean network of elevators, trapdoors, and cages beneath the wooden arena floor allowed beasts and gladiators to appear instantly before the crowd.",
