            "en": "Today, climate scientists closely monitor the Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation (AMOC) for signs of systemic collapse. Accelerating meltwater runoff from the Greenland ice sheet pours millions of tons of buoyant freshwater into the North Atlantic, diluting surface salinity. If water becomes too light to sink, the great conveyor could stall, triggering catastrophic agricultural cooling in northern Europe and destabilizing monsoonal rainfall for billions of people in the tropics.",
