            "en": "On Christmas Day in 2021, an Ariane 5 rocket roared into the cloudy skies over French Guiana, launching the most complex scientific instrument ever built: the James Webb Space Telescope (JWST). A collaborative masterpiece between NASA, ESA, and CSA, Webb featured a 6.5-meter primary mirror consisting of eighteen gold-coated beryllium hexagons, far too large to fit inside any existing rocket payload fairing.",
