            "en": "In ancient Greece, cities like Athens and Sparta were often locked in bitter conflict. Yet every fourth summer, bronze heralds traveled across mountains and valleys announcing the Olympic truce. For three months, warriors set aside their weapons so competitors could travel safely to the fertile plain of Olympia.",
