            "en": "Unlike American secularism, which shields religious expression from state interference, French laïcité shields the public sphere and public schools from religious pressure. By insisting that in the eyes of the law, every person is exclusively an equal citizen rather than a member of a competing ethnic or sectarian group, laïcité remains the sacred constitutional armor protecting French democratic unity.",
