            "paraNumber": 1,
            "en": "Originating in the craggy elevations of the Tibetan Plateau and carving an intricate course through friable loess sediment, the Yellow River constitutes the ecological backbone of northern Chinese civilization. While the torrential river carried catastrophic sediment loads that earned it the grim moniker 'China's Sorrow,' its recurrent depositions transformed the North China Plain into an extraordinarily fertile alluvial floodplain. Sedentary Neolithic populations harnessed this mineral-rich terrain to cultivate hardy millets and, eventually, wetland rice varieties.",
