            "paraNumber": 1,
            "en": "During the tumultuous twilight of the Warring States period, the western peripheral state of Qin appeared culturally unrefined and geopolitically isolated compared to the sophisticated kingdoms of the eastern plains. However, the appointment of Shang Yang as chief chancellor ignited the most radical socioeconomic overhaul in pre-modern history. Rejecting traditional Confucian ancestral etiquette and hereditary feudal entitlement, Shang Yang promulgated an uncompromising Legalist doctrine grounded in absolute codification, collective culpability, and state-mandated agrarian productivity.",
