            "paraNumber": 1,
            "en": "When King Ying Zheng proclaimed himself Qin Shi Huang—the First Sovereign Emperor—in 221 BCE, he executed an unprecedented homogenization of human activity across millions of square kilometers. Beyond annexing rival territories by force of arms, the regime imposed absolute standardization upon Chinese civilization: small-seal script unified divergent regional dialects into a universally legible written medium; uniform bronze weights and circular copper coins replaced regional barter discrepancies; even chariot axle gauges were standardized so that cartwheels wore identical ruts into trans-continental imperial highways.",
