            "paraNumber": 2,
            "en": "The velocity of development in Shenzhen was unprecedented, giving rise to the national catchphrase 'Shenzhen speed'—where high-rise factories and residential towers rose at a rate of one floor every three days. During his pivotal 1992 Southern Tour (Nanxun), Deng reaffirmed this market orientation against conservative ideological hardliners, cementing China's definitive entry into global capitalism. When China officially joined the World Trade Organization (WTO) in 2001, this infrastructure underpinned the greatest economic expansion in human history, lifting over eight hundred million citizens out of extreme poverty.",
