            "en": "In the span of a single generation, the People's Republic of China constructed the most gargantuan transportation network in human engineering history: over forty-five thousand kilometers of dedicated high-speed rail (HSR). This vast subterranean and viaduct web, accounting for more than two-thirds of the planet's total high-speed trackage, operates electric bullet trains traversing permafrost mountain tunnels in Tibet and sweltering tropical plains in Hainan at sustained speeds exceeding 350 kilometers per hour. What required days of arduous travel during the early reform era is now accomplished within hours.",
